WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.477 --> 00:00:16.258
I woke up the next morning, I could hear Mom in the kitchen.

2
00:00:18.239 --> 00:00:19.439
I sniffed the air.

3
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.381
Mmm Pancakes!

4
00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:26.142
Tate was already at the table, eating breakfast.

5
00:00:26.162 --> 00:00:28.583
"Hey," I said.

6
00:00:28.603 --> 00:00:30.604
"Save some pancakes for me!"

7
00:00:31.892 --> 00:00:33.073
Tate made a face at me.

8
00:00:33.093 --> 00:00:36.435
"Iggy," said Mom with a frown.

9
00:00:36.455 --> 00:00:38.896
"Please say good morning to your brother."

10
00:00:38.916 --> 00:00:42.298
"But Mom," I started to argue.

11
00:00:42.318 --> 00:00:48.041
"He made a face–" Before I could finish telling her, the telephone rang.

12
00:00:49.562 --> 00:00:50.683
Then the doorbell rang.

13
00:00:52.143 --> 00:00:53.584
My mom answered the telephone.

14
00:00:53.604 --> 00:00:57.226
"What?" she said, sounding surprised.

15
00:00:57.246 --> 00:00:59.848
"Really? How wonderful!"

16
00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:01.801
I answered the door.

17
00:01:02.481 --> 00:01:03.622
It was Josh and Jenny.

18
00:01:03.642 --> 00:01:06.964
"You'll never guess what happened!"

19
00:01:07.365 --> 00:01:08.125
Jenny cried.

20
00:01:08.145 --> 00:01:11.007
I could hear Mom in the kitchen.

21
00:01:11.027 --> 00:01:13.489
"Wait until I tell Iggy!"

22
00:01:13.869 --> 00:01:14.369
she said.

23
00:01:14.389 --> 00:01:16.691
"He'll be so excited!"

24
00:01:17.812 --> 00:01:19.553
So much was happening at once.

25
00:01:19.573 --> 00:01:22.355
"Bunch's ticket won the raffle!"

26
00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:23.656
said Josh.

27
00:01:23.676 --> 00:01:30.756
"We got a telephone call this morning from a hotel— the Shadow Lake Lodge," added Jenny.

28
00:01:30.776 --> 00:01:33.978
"We're all going to the mountain getaway!"

29
00:01:35.278 --> 00:01:37.979
I was so surprised, my mouth fell open.

30
00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:39.640
"Oh boy!"

31
00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:40.621
I whooped.

32
00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:44.822
"Molly and Caswell can come too," said Josh.

33
00:01:44.842 --> 00:01:46.563
"That makes six.

34
00:01:46.903 --> 00:01:48.524
Plus Bunch because he's the winner!"

35
00:01:48.544 --> 00:01:54.386
"The Lodge said we have to keep him in a dog cage in our room," said Jenny.

36
00:01:55.587 --> 00:01:57.908
Josh, Jenny, and I ran into the kitchen.

37
00:01:59.084 --> 00:02:01.405
"Thank you for calling," my mom was saying.

38
00:02:01.425 --> 00:02:04.085
"The kids will be so excited."

39
00:02:05.146 --> 00:02:06.406
She hung up the telephone.

40
00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:08.166
"That was Mr.

41
00:02:08.206 --> 00:02:09.567
Chen," she said.

42
00:02:09.587 --> 00:02:14.628
"You're all going–" "To the mountain getaway!"

43
00:02:15.088 --> 00:02:17.489
Josh, Jenny, and I cried at the same time.

44
00:02:17.509 --> 00:02:21.570
"Yes," said Mom, laughing.

45
00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:25.891
"Bunch's raffle ticket was chosen, so he's the winner!"

46
00:02:25.911 --> 00:02:28.652
"Which means we're the winners!"

47
00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:29.648
I said.

48
00:02:29.668 --> 00:02:34.590
"My dad says we can go next weekend," said Jenny.

49
00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:38.971
At that moment the wheels in my head started to turn.

50
00:02:39.891 --> 00:02:42.392
I needed an idea for a new invention.

51
00:02:42.412 --> 00:02:46.453
I wanted it to be a special invention for our mountain getaway.

52
00:02:46.473 --> 00:02:51.534
"Mom, Iggy's getting weird again," said Tate.

53
00:02:51.554 --> 00:02:53.795
"He's got that look on his face."

54
00:02:53.815 --> 00:02:55.776
"What look?"

55
00:02:56.216 --> 00:02:56.896
asked Josh.

56
00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:02.063
"The look that means he's about to make a huge mess," said Tate.

57
00:03:03.063 --> 00:03:03.864
Mom laughed.

58
00:03:03.884 --> 00:03:07.546
"Iggy's probably thinking up a new invention."

59
00:03:07.566 --> 00:03:12.769
"Which means he's about to make a mess, just like I said!"

60
00:03:13.189 --> 00:03:13.850
said Tate.

61
00:03:15.071 --> 00:03:17.092
He grinned and punched me in the arm.

62
00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:19.693
I punched him back playfully.

63
00:03:20.274 --> 00:03:23.536
"Tate really isn't such a bad brother," I thought.

64
00:03:24.532 --> 00:03:27.855
Maybe we wouldn't fight as much now that we didn't share a room anymore.

65
00:03:29.096 --> 00:03:32.399
Josh, Jenny, and I ran over to Molly and Caswell's apartment.

66
00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:35.321
We wanted to tell them the big news.

67
00:03:35.341 --> 00:03:38.544
"Wow!" said Molly.

68
00:03:38.564 --> 00:03:41.506
"I'm going to bring my new sleeping bag!"

69
00:03:42.587 --> 00:03:45.289
"I'm going to bring my backpack," said Caswell.

70
00:03:45.309 --> 00:03:47.171
"And my flashlight.

71
00:03:47.411 --> 00:03:49.873
We might get lost in the woods in the middle of the night."

72
00:03:52.115 --> 00:03:53.096
We all laughed.

73
00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:57.261
"I don't think we're going to get lost in the woods," said Josh.

74
00:03:57.281 --> 00:03:59.842
"Especially in the middle of the night."

75
00:04:00.842 --> 00:04:03.483
Suddenly the wheels in my head started spinning again.

76
00:04:04.263 --> 00:04:07.204
But this time my mind went click!

77
00:04:08.724 --> 00:04:11.765
Now I had an idea for my new invention!

78
00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:15.086
I didn't tell anyone about it—not yet.

79
00:04:16.126 --> 00:04:18.347
First I had to see how it was going to work.

80
00:04:19.347 --> 00:04:22.188
I started by borrowing hamster pellets from Josh.

81
00:04:23.528 --> 00:04:25.951
Next I asked Mom for some food coloring.

82
00:04:26.771 --> 00:04:30.235
She gave me red, green, blue, and yellow.

83
00:04:31.456 --> 00:04:34.118
Then I went into my room and closed the door.

84
00:04:35.679 --> 00:04:39.663
I, Iggy, was about to invent something that would amaze the world.

85
00:04:40.904 --> 00:04:44.428
And it would keep people from getting stranded in the mountains!
